 "prompt": "The repository at /testbed has a bug, described below. Fix it by changing the source code; do not modify or\nadd tests. When you are done, the project's existing test suite should pass.\n\n<issue>\nTable cell navigation returns wrong row when accessing row above\n\n#### Description\n\nWhen trying to access the row above a table cell using the `_tr_above` property, the method returns incorrect results or raises unexpected errors. The navigation logic appears to be looking in the wrong direction.\n\n#### Steps/Code to Reproduce\n\n```python\nfrom docx import Document\nfrom docx.oxml.table import CT_Tbl\nfrom docx.oxml.parser import parse_xml\n\n# Create a simple table with multiple rows\ndoc = Document()\ntable = doc.add_table(rows=3, cols=2)\n\n# Try to access the row above from a cell in the second row\n# This should work but currently fails\ncell = table.rows[1].cells[0]\ntry:\n    # This should return the first row but doesn't work correctly\n    above_row = cell._element._tr_above\n    print(f\"Found row above: {above_row}\")\nexcept Exception as e:\n    print(f\"Error accessing row above: {e}\")\n\n# Also fails when trying to access from top row (should raise ValueError)\ntop_cell = table.rows[0].cells[0]\ntry:\n    above_row = top_cell._element._tr_above\n    print(\"This shouldn't work - no row above top row\")\nexcept ValueError as e:\n    print(f\"Expected error: {e}\")\n```\n\nThe `_tr_above` property on table cells is not working as expected. When called on cells that should have a row above them, it either returns None or raises incorrect errors. When called on cells in the topmost row, it should raise a ValueError but the behavior is inconsistent.\n</issue>\n",
